        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Explain why all integers are rational numbers.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Every integer can be written as a fraction with a denominator of $1$.",
          "worked": "Any integer $n$ can be written as $\\frac{n}{1}$. Both $n$ and $1$ are integers, and the denominator is non-zero, so every integer is rational.",
